"""FTSH-105-01-L-DV-K-A-P-TR — Samtec 2x5 1.27 mm SMD pin header with alignment pegs.

Generic 10-pin (2 rows × 5 positions) surface-mount pin header on 1.27 mm
(0.050") pitch, widely used as the ARM Cortex Debug / SWD+JTAG connector
and other keyed 10-pin interfaces.

Suffix decode (Samtec FTSH-105-01-L-DV-K-A-P-TR)
  FTSH  0.050" terminal strip, SMD pin header
  105   5 pins per row (10 pins total)
  01    (3.05 mm) .120" post (mates with FFSD-series socket)
  L     0.160" nominal mating post height variant
  DV    double-row, vertical (SMT)
  K     keying shroud (plastic polarizer for mating with FFSD)
  A     alignment pin (the two mechanical through-hole pegs)
  P     molded pick-&-place pad on the top of the shroud
  -TR   tape and reel

Mechanical
- Two NPTH alignment holes at x = ±1.90 mm (1.1 mm drill) accept the
  "-A" alignment pegs. They are mechanical only — leave unconnected.
- Pin numbering: odd pins on one row (1, 3, 5, 7, 9), even pins on the
  other (2, 4, 6, 8, 10). Pin 1 is marked with a small filled triangle
  on F.SilkS next to pad 1.

Cortex Debug (ARM 10-pin) mapping, for reference:
    1 VTref       2 SWDIO/TMS
    3 GND         4 SWCLK/TCK
    5 GND         6 SWO/TDO
    7 KEY(NC)     8 NC/TDI
    9 GNDDetect  10 nRESET
"""

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)
P3 = io(Net)
P4 = io(Net)
P5 = io(Net)
P6 = io(Net)
P7 = io(Net)
P8 = io(Net)
P9 = io(Net)
P10 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="J",
    symbol=Symbol(library="FTSH-105-01-L-DV-K-A-P-TR.kicad_sym"),
    pins={
        "1": P1,
        "2": P2,
        "3": P3,
        "4": P4,
        "5": P5,
        "6": P6,
        "7": P7,
        "8": P8,
        "9": P9,
        "10": P10,
    },
)
